About the book
In "Fortune's Formula," William Poundstone delves into the
fascinating and high-stakes world of gambling, investing, and
probability theory, uncovering the mathematical secret known
as the Kelly criterion. This ingenious formula, pioneered by
John Kelly at Bell Labs, holds the promise of optimizing bets
and investments to maximize wealth over the long term,
blending elegance with an aura of mystery. Through riveting
anecdotes featuring larger-than-life characters—some of
history's greatest gamblers, investors, and
scientists—Poundstone not only demystifies this potent blend
of science and strategy but also brings to light the intense
intrigues and ethical dilemmas faced by those who wield its
power. Whether you are an avid follower of Wall Street, a
mathematics enthusiast, or simply someone captivated by the
adrenaline of high-risk ventures, this book invites you to
explore how a single formula can alter your perception of risk,
reward, and the very essence of financial success.
